From: Jason Penilla <11360596+jpenilla@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:38:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Rework map holder tracking

Vanilla updates every holder of a map from each holder's tick by scanning
the other holders' inventories, and carriers remove frame viewers that don't
have the map in their inventory, so frame viewers are constantly dropped and
re-added and receive the full map again on every frame update.

A player is now a holder of a map while the map is in their inventory or
equipment, or while a frame showing it is tracking them, and each player
only updates their own holder:

- Inventory: a map ticked from the player's inventory/equipment marks them
  as carrying it and updates only their own marker. Maps that were not
  ticked by the end of aiStep have left the inventory. This replaces the
  drop hook. Spectators whose tick is skipped in unloaded chunks still
  update the maps they carry.
- Frames: players are subscribed when they start tracking the frame and
  sent the full map immediately, and unsubscribed when tracking stops or
  the frame's map changes. Viewers now only receive the full map again
  when they start tracking the frame again, instead of on every frame
  update while anyone carries the map. Frame markers are ticked once per
  frame instead of once per viewer.
- Map invisibility equipment hides the wearer's marker per viewer; the
  wearer still sees themselves.
- Leaving a world only visits the player's own maps instead of every
  loaded map.

Player markers are no longer copied to locked maps: they are live state, and
copies were either replaced immediately or left stale forever.

Behaviour changes:
- A cancelled PlayerTrackEntityEvent for an item frame also withholds that
  frame's map contents.
- With item-frame-cursor-update-interval <= 0, viewers get the map once
  when they start tracking the frame, and no updates after.
- Moving a map with the inventory cursor causes one full resend (the cursor
  is not ticked).
- NMS: tickCarriedBy lost its frame parameter (frames use tickFrame),
  getHoldingPlayer throws, and carriedBy/carriedByPlayers include
  frame-only viewers.

